\ Not supported yet (490; the coordinator's rule): a brace that is a
\ have-by's whole body, inside try. Pinned Lean logs its error (the brace
\ sees Tactic.run's recover, true: observed, lfr-whole? in tactic-run.fs;
\ review tb2-blocks3's re-check) and rejects; a later failing step inside
\ the try could take the message back, so LeanForth answers 490, never
\ accepted. Its bullet twin `by · exact h` throws and Lean accepts: 490
\ refuses neither wrongly. Lean twin u_try_have_brace in blocks-3-wrong.lean.
\ Lean: theorem u_try_have_brace (a b : Nat) (h : a = b) (k : b = a) : a = b := by
\         try (have j : b = a := by { exact h })
\         exact h
theorem u_try_have_brace
  Nat explicit: a  Nat explicit: b
  a b = explicit: h  b a = explicit: k
  a b =
:= by
  by-try b a = by-have-by: j { ' h by-exact } by-end by-end
  ' h by-exact
end u_try_have_brace
